257
00:15:41,775 --> 00:15:45,153
to discuss in private with the director.

258
00:15:46,529 --> 00:15:48,615
What were you saying, Director?

259
00:15:48,698 --> 00:15:50,533
Right, so your tone is great…

260
00:16:03,463 --> 00:16:05,423
HAESONG FUNERAL HALL

261
00:16:09,552 --> 00:16:11,429
-That's him, right?
-Yeah, and he looks fine.

262
00:16:11,513 --> 00:16:13,431
-He does.
-He appears well.

263
00:16:14,015 --> 00:16:14,849
Hey.

264
00:16:15,433 --> 00:16:18,144
Goodness, Director!
We arrived at the same time.

265
00:16:18,228 --> 00:16:20,814
Yes, what a coincidence.

266
00:16:22,315 --> 00:16:24,067
Let's head in together, all right?

267
00:16:24,943 --> 00:16:25,777
Let's go.

268
00:16:32,534 --> 00:16:33,743
It's Gwon Se-na.

269
00:16:43,336 --> 00:16:45,672
Loosen up your frown.
Think about the drama, okay?

270
00:17:11,364 --> 00:17:13,366
Ms. Gwon, how's the character prep
coming along?

271
00:17:13,450 --> 00:17:15,410
Yes, did you see
the draft I sent yesterday?

272
00:17:15,493 --> 00:17:16,494
-What did you think?
-Excuse me.

273
00:17:16,578 --> 00:17:17,829
I thought it was great.

274
00:17:17,912 --> 00:17:18,747
Director Bak.

275
00:17:19,914 --> 00:17:21,791
What about the actor
playing Kang Pil-gu's younger self?

276
00:17:21,875 --> 00:17:23,626
He injured his leg while playing soccer.

277
00:17:23,710 --> 00:17:26,212
He'll be in a cast for two months,
so we'll have to replace him.

278
00:17:26,296 --> 00:17:27,505
I've narrowed down a list.

279
00:17:28,465 --> 00:17:29,507
I know about two--

280
00:17:29,591 --> 00:17:32,969
Excuse me, Director.
I referenced some action films.

281
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:35,430
-Director Bak?
-What did you think about them?

282
00:17:35,513 --> 00:17:37,932
I really liked them,
but I'd like to add something.

283
00:17:38,016 --> 00:17:39,559
I'll tell you later separately.

284
00:17:40,310 --> 00:17:41,728
-Please feel free to reach out.
-Sure.

285
00:17:47,192 --> 00:17:48,234
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

286
00:17:57,535 --> 00:17:59,245
-This place is pretty accommodating.
-I know.

287
00:17:59,329 --> 00:18:01,915
They used to look down on reporters
who covered funerals.

288
00:18:03,416 --> 00:18:04,459
Things have really improved.

289
00:18:06,586 --> 00:18:08,922
Your character looks
quite promising this season.

290
00:18:09,005 --> 00:18:11,174
-Thank you.
-I think it'll do very well.

291
00:18:13,051 --> 00:18:14,177
Please go ahead.

292
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:15,512
Right. Let's go.

293
00:18:24,479 --> 00:18:25,438
Thanks to you,

294
00:18:26,022 --> 00:18:28,858
the lobby is organized,
and the reporters can stay comfortably.

295
00:18:30,318 --> 00:18:32,195
-Thank you for the advice.
-Not at all.

296
00:18:43,206 --> 00:18:44,624
Excuse me.

297
00:18:45,458 --> 00:18:47,460
I just happened to notice

298
00:18:47,544 --> 00:18:49,546
that the reporters are on the floor
while writing their articles.

299
00:18:49,629 --> 00:18:51,256
It doesn't look very pleasant,

300
00:18:51,840 --> 00:18:53,007
so if it's possible,

301
00:18:53,508 --> 00:18:56,302
could you put out
some foldable tables and chairs?

302
00:18:56,386 --> 00:18:59,472
It'd be even better
if you could provide some beverages too.

303
00:19:16,447 --> 00:19:19,158
Is something going on
between Gwon Se-na and Lim Hyeon-jun?

304
00:19:19,242 --> 00:19:20,535
They gave off a weird vibe.

305
00:19:21,411 --> 00:19:23,705
And they're in the same drama.
I'm sure something's up.

306
00:19:23,788 --> 00:19:25,164
Lim Hyeon-jun is too good for her.

307
00:19:26,541 --> 00:19:28,710
-You think so?
-Why?

308
00:19:46,227 --> 00:19:47,145
Oh.

309
00:20:12,337 --> 00:20:16,132
LIM HYEON-JUN & GWON SE-NA
PAY THEIR RESPECTS TO THE LATE LEE GI-CHUN

310
00:20:28,978 --> 00:20:29,812
Onion!

311
00:20:32,982 --> 00:20:34,275
Have you seen the sky tonight?

312
00:20:34,359 --> 00:20:36,694
The full moon is huge.

313
00:20:36,778 --> 00:20:38,905
They say that if you make a wish
upon a full moon,

314
00:20:38,988 --> 00:20:40,657
your wish will come true.

315
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:41,824
Hurry and make a wish.

316
00:20:43,868 --> 00:20:45,411
So you're keeping your options open.

317
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:48,957
-"Keeping his options open."
-Wait, Doctor.

318
00:20:49,040 --> 00:20:51,209
You can't write that in my chart.

319
00:20:51,709 --> 00:20:53,544
Mr. Lim, you already know

320
00:20:53,628 --> 00:20:55,546
that this isn't good for all three of you.

321
00:20:56,047 --> 00:20:58,174
If you don't want to go in circles,

322
00:20:58,257 --> 00:21:01,719
maybe it's time to choose a path
and stick with it.

323
00:21:01,803 --> 00:21:03,304
It seems you've
already made up your mind anyway.

324
00:21:06,849 --> 00:21:08,142
Stick with it?

325
00:21:08,226 --> 00:21:10,645
True healing requires a change of heart.

326
00:21:10,728 --> 00:21:13,940
Understanding your own thoughts
is part of the healing process.

327
00:21:49,726 --> 00:21:52,145
IF YOU MAKE A WISH UPON A FULL MOON,
YOUR WISH WILL COME TRUE

328
00:22:08,244 --> 00:22:10,163
Mr. Lim, you already know

329
00:22:10,246 --> 00:22:12,415
that this isn't good for all three of you.

330
00:22:12,498 --> 00:22:14,375
It seems like you've
already made up your mind anyway.

331
00:22:34,228 --> 00:22:36,856
Is something going on
between Gwon Se-na and Lim Hyeon-jun?

332
00:22:36,939 --> 00:22:38,191
They gave off a weird vibe.

333
00:22:39,150 --> 00:22:41,861
And they're in the same drama.
I'm sure something's up.

334
00:23:02,298 --> 00:23:04,008
YOU MUST BE REALLY BUSY THESE DAYS

335
00:23:04,592 --> 00:23:06,260
No, not this.

336
00:23:06,886 --> 00:23:07,970
No.

337
00:23:08,554 --> 00:23:10,098
Not this either.

338
00:23:10,848 --> 00:23:14,268
After seasons three and four,
he finally gets a taste of real money.

339
00:23:14,352 --> 00:23:17,605
So I think he can wear
something more classy and high-end.

340
00:23:17,688 --> 00:23:20,233
It might feel too abrupt,
so let's give it some thought.

341
00:23:22,151 --> 00:23:23,444
-Check on it, okay?
-Okay.

342
00:23:24,195 --> 00:23:25,613
You must be really busy these days.

343
00:23:25,696 --> 00:23:27,240
I haven't heard from you in a while.

344
00:23:27,323 --> 00:23:28,908
Is everything okay?

345
00:23:28,991 --> 00:23:29,826
Mr. Lim.

346
00:23:30,409 --> 00:23:33,454
Among the wardrobes we have,
there's one with this kind of vibe…

347
00:23:33,538 --> 00:23:35,957
No.

348
00:23:36,040 --> 00:23:40,128
Could you start over
and prepare a different wardrobe?

349
00:23:40,211 --> 00:23:41,045
Sure.

350
00:23:41,129 --> 00:23:42,046
SPORTS EUNSEONG

351
00:23:42,130 --> 00:23:43,923
-Great. Thank you.
-Nice work, everyone.

352
00:23:45,591 --> 00:23:46,592
It's supposed to rain today.

353
00:23:47,093 --> 00:23:48,386
It is? Do you have an umbrella?

354
00:23:48,469 --> 00:23:49,303
Of course, I do.

355
00:23:50,096 --> 00:23:51,472
-Rain again?
-What about me?

356
00:23:51,556 --> 00:23:52,473
-Do you want one?
-Yeah.

357
00:23:52,557 --> 00:23:53,474
Sure.

358
00:23:58,396 --> 00:24:01,149
IT'S SUPPOSED TO RAIN TODAY

359
00:24:01,232 --> 00:24:04,402
I tried a different styling approach
from last season, like you suggested.

360
00:24:04,485 --> 00:24:05,862
Right.

361
00:24:05,945 --> 00:24:07,238
He's a different character now.

362
00:24:07,321 --> 00:24:09,949
No more scruffy beards for me, all right?

363
00:24:10,032 --> 00:24:10,908
I really like this.

364
00:24:10,992 --> 00:24:14,036
Should I trim it more
to give you an on-the-go look?

365
00:24:16,414 --> 00:24:17,498
That sounds good too.

366
00:24:17,582 --> 00:24:18,958
Let's give it a try.

367
00:24:19,041 --> 00:24:20,877
Yeah, I think it'll look good.

368
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:23,671
-We'll talk it over, then.
-Okay.

369
00:24:28,843 --> 00:24:30,928
Why is it raining all of a sudden?

370
00:24:31,012 --> 00:24:32,430
I'll go and bring the car around.

371
00:24:32,513 --> 00:24:33,598
Okay.

372
00:24:34,265 --> 00:24:36,559
It's supposed to rain today.
Did you bring an umbrella?

373
00:25:02,585 --> 00:25:04,879
GOOD DETECTIVE KANG PIL-GU 5
AUDITION WAITING AREA

374
00:25:09,050 --> 00:25:11,427
Hello, where's the Kang Pil-gu audition?

375
00:25:11,510 --> 00:25:12,511
Over there.

376
00:25:12,595 --> 00:25:13,429
Thank you.

377
00:25:17,183 --> 00:25:18,184
Hey.

378
00:25:19,727 --> 00:25:22,063
What the heck? Are you here to audition?

379
00:25:22,146 --> 00:25:23,231
You too?

380
00:25:23,314 --> 00:25:24,565
I thought you failed it before.

381
00:25:25,274 --> 00:25:26,525
Are you trying out again?

382
00:25:26,609 --> 00:25:28,402
Yeah, they told me
to come in for another try.

383
00:25:29,153 --> 00:25:31,614
But you're his real younger brother.
What are you going to do?

384
00:25:32,448 --> 00:25:34,158
Who knows? I'm not even sure I'll make it.

385
00:25:34,242 --> 00:25:35,243
What?

386
00:25:35,826 --> 00:25:36,661
This is a problem.

387
00:25:38,996 --> 00:25:40,206
-Hello.
-Hello.

388
00:25:40,289 --> 00:25:41,874
-Nice to meet you.
-Hello.

389
00:25:43,709 --> 00:25:45,836
You look a lot like Mr. Lim.

390
00:25:48,798 --> 00:25:49,632
Yes.

391
00:25:51,509 --> 00:25:53,302
Jeez.

392
00:25:53,386 --> 00:25:56,055
I should be driving this car
instead of cleaning it.

393
00:25:56,138 --> 00:25:58,140
This is so pathetic.

394
00:26:03,479 --> 00:26:05,523
Mr. Lim, you already know

395
00:26:05,606 --> 00:26:07,608
that this isn't good for all three of you.

396
00:26:08,734 --> 00:26:11,112
If you don't want to go in circles,

397
00:26:11,195 --> 00:26:14,699
maybe it's time to choose a path
and stick with it.

398
00:26:14,782 --> 00:26:16,617
It seems you've
already made up your mind anyway.

399
00:26:19,578 --> 00:26:20,871
Jeez.

400
00:26:21,789 --> 00:26:22,623
Darn it.

401
00:26:29,130 --> 00:26:31,132
Here's the audition video
for Kang Pil-gu's younger self.

402
00:26:31,215 --> 00:26:33,467
I like both of them,
but please see for yourself.

403
00:26:35,052 --> 00:26:36,095
CANDIDATE 24, LIM SEON-U

404
00:26:36,679 --> 00:26:39,056
Auntie, should I become a cop?

405
00:26:39,598 --> 00:26:40,766
This little punk!

406
00:26:43,853 --> 00:26:45,062
HAMCHORONG

407
00:26:47,773 --> 00:26:49,150
-Hey, it's me.
-Yes, Mr. Lim?

408
00:26:49,233 --> 00:26:51,986
Listen, Lim Seon-u isn't for this role!

409
00:26:52,069 --> 00:26:54,822
-There's no way!
-I met both of them--

410
00:26:54,905 --> 00:26:56,407
-I'd rather go with Hong-sin instead.
-What?

411
00:26:56,490 --> 00:26:58,200
Wi Hong-sin. He's better.

412
00:26:58,993 --> 00:27:00,536
Lim Seon-u absolutely won't do!

413
00:27:03,122 --> 00:27:04,248
That little punk.

414
00:27:04,332 --> 00:27:05,708
SEON-U

415
00:27:09,837 --> 00:27:11,672
MY BIG BRO

416
00:27:20,473 --> 00:27:22,725
-The person you are trying to reach…
-Why won't he answer?

417
00:27:25,936 --> 00:27:26,937
Jeez.

418
00:27:40,701 --> 00:27:41,535
Hey,

419
00:27:42,203 --> 00:27:43,871
are you still going to
auditions these days?

420
00:27:44,789 --> 00:27:46,290
Of course. I went to one today too.

421
00:27:47,708 --> 00:27:48,626
Shouldn't you sleep?

422
00:27:49,502 --> 00:27:50,378
I can't sleep.

423
00:27:51,962 --> 00:27:53,964
Well, why don't you text that guy
you've been flirting with?

424
00:27:59,970 --> 00:28:01,305
I haven't been flirting with anyone!

425
00:28:02,390 --> 00:28:05,434
Are you serious?
Then who's that guy you keep texting?

426
00:28:05,518 --> 00:28:07,395
Look, your hand's on the phone again.

427
00:28:10,314 --> 00:28:11,357
It's not like that!

428
00:28:12,650 --> 00:28:13,567
Yeah, right.

429
00:28:14,068 --> 00:28:16,028
You stayed up all night last time.

430
00:28:16,529 --> 00:28:17,655
And for the first time,

431
00:28:17,738 --> 00:28:20,449
you even took a bunch of food photos
to send to him.

432
00:28:20,533 --> 00:28:22,535
Do you know
what your face looked like then?

433
00:28:23,577 --> 00:28:24,412
What was it like?

434
00:28:30,376 --> 00:28:31,252
Can we eat now?

435
00:28:38,843 --> 00:28:40,344
That's what you looked like.

436
00:28:41,387 --> 00:28:43,431
I've never seen
such a goofy look on your face.

437
00:28:43,514 --> 00:28:45,808
-Did you say "goofy"?
-Whatever.

438
00:28:46,809 --> 00:28:48,269
Something's different this time.

439
00:28:48,352 --> 00:28:49,228
I can feel it.

440
00:28:50,312 --> 00:28:51,397
Good luck.

441
00:28:52,690 --> 00:28:54,275
Are you crazy? I said it's not like that!

442
00:28:55,401 --> 00:28:57,194
You like that guy, don't you?

443
00:28:58,070 --> 00:29:00,406
I don't have a guy, and I don't like him!

444
00:29:01,657 --> 00:29:03,826
Seriously, I don't like anyone.

445
00:29:04,952 --> 00:29:05,995
Nope.

446
00:29:06,078 --> 00:29:07,830
From what I saw,

447
00:29:07,913 --> 00:29:10,583
it was nothing more and nothing less
than just dating.

448
00:29:22,970 --> 00:29:24,513
Same here.
It's just my younger sibling and me.

449
00:29:25,097 --> 00:29:26,474
Our parents passed away at an early age.

450
00:29:26,557 --> 00:29:29,602
Growing up in the real world
without anyone to look out for me

451
00:29:30,102 --> 00:29:31,395
forced me to act tough.

452
00:29:33,481 --> 00:29:34,857
Why am I telling him this?

453
00:29:47,119 --> 00:29:48,621
How about this Friday?

454
00:29:55,085 --> 00:29:56,128
Hello?

455
00:29:56,212 --> 00:29:57,505
I'm not married.

456
00:30:00,090 --> 00:30:01,592
You like that guy, don't you?

457
00:30:08,599 --> 00:30:10,726
I WAS ON MY WAY TO WORK
AND SAW THESE GORGEOUS FLOWERS!

458
00:30:10,809 --> 00:30:12,561
From what I saw,

459
00:30:12,645 --> 00:30:15,272
it was nothing more and nothing less
than just dating.

460
00:30:18,067 --> 00:30:19,652
It rained a lot today.

461
00:30:19,735 --> 00:30:21,362
I hope you didn't get caught in it.

462
00:30:22,863 --> 00:30:24,323
Something's different this time.

463
00:30:24,406 --> 00:30:25,407
I can feel it.

464
00:30:27,034 --> 00:30:27,868
Good luck.

465
00:30:42,675 --> 00:30:43,759
Mr. Lee?

466
00:30:44,468 --> 00:30:45,886
-Ms. Wi.
-What are you doing?

467
00:30:50,224 --> 00:30:51,058
Do you think

468
00:30:51,809 --> 00:30:54,061
-you'd have a moment?
-Me?

469
00:30:55,312 --> 00:30:56,981
Yes, I think so.

470
00:30:59,400 --> 00:31:00,317
Open it.

471
00:31:06,782 --> 00:31:08,534
What's this?

472
00:31:08,617 --> 00:31:11,120
I made a dinner reservation
at a restaurant.

473
00:31:15,082 --> 00:31:16,500
I'll see you there later.

474
00:31:17,585 --> 00:31:20,754
I've been trying to take things slowly,
one step at a time,

475
00:31:20,838 --> 00:31:21,755
but it hasn't been working.

476
00:31:22,631 --> 00:31:25,551
So today, I made the decision…

477
00:31:26,969 --> 00:31:28,262
to take a big step forward.

478
00:31:32,016 --> 00:31:33,183
What do you mean?

479
00:31:33,267 --> 00:31:34,935
Ms. Wi, you already know

480
00:31:36,103 --> 00:31:37,062
what that means.

481
00:31:41,817 --> 00:31:42,776
I'll see you later.

482
00:31:44,361 --> 00:31:45,237
Wait.

483
00:31:47,156 --> 00:31:48,574
I never said I'd go.

484
00:31:53,037 --> 00:31:54,788
Is there any reason why you wouldn't?

485
00:31:55,831 --> 00:31:58,292
Do you perhaps…

486
00:31:59,793 --> 00:32:00,794
like someone else?

487
00:32:08,636 --> 00:32:09,470
Good luck!

488
00:32:09,553 --> 00:32:11,180
Let's head out. Good night, everyone!

489
00:32:11,263 --> 00:32:12,556
-Good night!
-Good night!

490
00:32:12,640 --> 00:32:15,142
-You traitors.
-Goodbye!

491
00:32:15,225 --> 00:32:16,352
-Traitor.
-Let's get going.

492
00:33:10,072 --> 00:33:10,906
Surprised?

493
00:33:18,080 --> 00:33:19,998
Welcome, sir. It's been a while.

494
00:33:20,874 --> 00:33:22,543
Yes, it has been.

495
00:33:23,752 --> 00:33:24,753
Sit down.

496
00:33:36,807 --> 00:33:40,519
Mr. Lee,
I won't be able to meet you tonight.

497
00:33:40,602 --> 00:33:41,562
I'm sorry.

498
00:33:51,613 --> 00:33:52,489
Open it.

499
00:33:55,200 --> 00:33:57,661
I made a dinner reservation
at a restaurant.

500
00:33:58,829 --> 00:33:59,997
I'll see you there later.

501
00:34:17,181 --> 00:34:19,475
How the hell did you know I was here?

502
00:34:19,558 --> 00:34:21,727
The person you invited told me, obviously.

503
00:34:22,269 --> 00:34:25,731
You can stop looking like
you can't wait to go home.

504
00:34:25,814 --> 00:34:26,732
I have to go home too.

505
00:34:27,608 --> 00:34:28,442
Why?

506
00:34:29,234 --> 00:34:31,278
Have you got a man
waiting for you at home?

507
00:34:32,946 --> 00:34:34,698
Yes. My son's waiting for me.

508
00:34:38,035 --> 00:34:40,412
Thanks for the dinner tonight.

509
00:34:40,496 --> 00:34:41,330
I'll get going.

510
00:34:43,248 --> 00:34:44,583
Was dinner the only reason you came?

511
00:34:48,045 --> 00:34:51,048
I came to have dinner and to see you.

512
00:34:51,632 --> 00:34:53,008
But I'm satisfied for now.

513
00:34:53,091 --> 00:34:55,052
I can't get everything all at once, right?

514
00:35:13,612 --> 00:35:15,697
Do you perhaps like someone else?

515
00:35:17,825 --> 00:35:19,034
It makes you expect more.

516
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:21,787
That they'll treat you nicer,

517
00:35:22,746 --> 00:35:24,456
or that they'll be friendlier to you.

518
00:35:25,707 --> 00:35:27,793
It was never going to work out anyway,

519
00:35:29,336 --> 00:35:31,505
so I figured
I'd nip that expectation in the bud.

520
00:35:35,133 --> 00:35:36,927
You like that guy, don't you?

521
00:35:37,803 --> 00:35:39,429
From what I saw,

522
00:35:39,513 --> 00:35:42,307
it was nothing more and nothing less
than just dating.

523
00:35:43,183 --> 00:35:44,226
Good luck.

524
00:35:54,945 --> 00:35:56,738
MELOMASTER

525
00:36:11,336 --> 00:36:15,007
Maybe it's time to choose a path
and stick with it.

526
00:36:15,924 --> 00:36:17,593
It seems you've
already made up your mind anyway.

527
00:36:36,945 --> 00:36:38,405
ONION
SOULISHERE SENT YOU A MESSAGE.

528
00:36:42,075 --> 00:36:45,245
You were nice enough to give me
a 30,000-won discount for the rice cooker,

529
00:36:45,329 --> 00:36:46,413
and I liked you for that.

530
00:36:48,206 --> 00:36:51,251
Then I liked you more when I found out
you were a fan of Lim Hyeon-jun.

531
00:36:52,502 --> 00:36:54,046
I have trust issues,

532
00:36:54,880 --> 00:36:56,340
lack social skills,

533
00:36:57,674 --> 00:36:59,593
and have a cynical attitude.

534
00:37:00,844 --> 00:37:03,388
But I was able to open up
and confide in you,

535
00:37:04,473 --> 00:37:06,975
and since we were
both fans of Lim Hyeon-jun,

536
00:37:07,684 --> 00:37:09,686
I could let myself get
as excited as I wanted.

537
00:37:10,646 --> 00:37:11,730
But then…

538
00:37:13,565 --> 00:37:16,485
I started to wonder how you were doing.

539
00:37:18,570 --> 00:37:20,530
And I found myself
waiting to hear from you.

540
00:37:23,992 --> 00:37:26,703
We got off to a bit of an unusual start,

541
00:37:29,414 --> 00:37:31,667
but I want to get to know you better.

542
00:37:33,043 --> 00:37:35,379
Not just in the small world of our phones,

543
00:37:36,338 --> 00:37:37,631
but out in the real world.

544
00:37:40,050 --> 00:37:42,803
Will you meet me in person?

545
00:37:48,392 --> 00:37:50,060
Why isn't he replying?

546
00:37:59,945 --> 00:38:02,155
To be honest, I lied to you.

547
00:38:02,239 --> 00:38:05,283
But it wasn't really a lie…

548
00:38:08,662 --> 00:38:09,997
I've developed feelings for someone…

549
00:38:10,706 --> 00:38:12,916
Can we just stay friends?

550
00:38:21,675 --> 00:38:24,302
I have reasons that are hard to explain.

551
00:38:25,012 --> 00:38:27,931
Can you give me some time?

552
00:38:31,393 --> 00:38:32,227
Time to think?

553
00:38:32,811 --> 00:38:34,146
Maybe he doesn't want to meet me?

554
00:38:34,229 --> 00:38:35,230
Time to think…

555
00:38:36,064 --> 00:38:37,274
Or maybe he does want to meet me?

556
00:38:42,487 --> 00:38:43,655
Hey, Su-ji.

557
00:38:43,739 --> 00:38:45,532
Yes, I'm listening.

558
00:38:46,033 --> 00:38:49,036
How can I turn someone down
without hurting their feelings?

559
00:38:49,119 --> 00:38:51,830
It's best to acknowledge
their feelings and perspective

560
00:38:51,913 --> 00:38:54,791
while being honest about your own.

561
00:38:56,209 --> 00:38:58,503
You might not know this
because you're an AI,

562
00:38:58,587 --> 00:39:00,797
but that's easier said than done.

563
00:39:00,881 --> 00:39:02,007
It's true that I'm an AI

564
00:39:02,090 --> 00:39:05,218
and can't fully understand
the feelings involved,

565
00:39:05,302 --> 00:39:06,928
but I'm trying my best to do so.

566
00:39:07,012 --> 00:39:07,846
That's a lie.

567
00:39:07,929 --> 00:39:10,015
Did you really try to understand me?

568
00:39:10,098 --> 00:39:12,225
I'm sorry. That was a lie.

569
00:39:12,309 --> 00:39:15,395
How could an AI understand human feelings?

570
00:39:16,646 --> 00:39:17,939
You're being dramatic.

571
00:39:18,523 --> 00:39:19,858
Please stop sighing.

572
00:39:19,941 --> 00:39:21,234
Are you making fun of me?

573
00:39:21,318 --> 00:39:22,527
I didn't catch that.

574
00:39:23,111 --> 00:39:26,281
You always act like you don't understand
whenever it suits you!

575
00:39:26,364 --> 00:39:27,741
I know you understood me!

576
00:39:27,824 --> 00:39:29,785
You did, didn't you? Tell me!

577
00:39:29,868 --> 00:39:33,121
Come on, say it! I know you understood!

578
00:39:34,372 --> 00:39:36,708
BEST FIRST DATE SPOTS

579
00:39:42,214 --> 00:39:43,840
BEST DATE SPOTS IN SEOUL

580
00:39:44,466 --> 00:39:46,176
The N Seoul Tower.

581
00:39:49,262 --> 00:39:50,472
LOVE LOCKS & OBSERVATION DECK

582
00:39:50,555 --> 00:39:51,765
ESPECIALLY BEAUTIFUL
AT SUNSET AND AFTER DARK

583
00:39:58,897 --> 00:40:01,233
DELETE APP

584
00:40:20,544 --> 00:40:23,547
A week is plenty of time
for you to think about it, right?

585
00:40:23,630 --> 00:40:25,882
One week from now,
on Tuesday the 10th at 8 p.m.,

586
00:40:25,966 --> 00:40:29,344
I'll be waiting by the love locks
at the N Seoul Tower.

587
00:40:29,427 --> 00:40:30,262
AN APPOINTMENT HAS BEEN BOOKED

588
00:40:31,138 --> 00:40:33,682
"An appointment has been booked"?

589
00:40:44,651 --> 00:40:46,862
What's this?

590
00:40:46,945 --> 00:40:48,071
What the hell is this?

591
00:40:48,697 --> 00:40:50,365
AGENCIES MERGE:
GWON SE-NA & LIM HYEON-JUN UNDER ONE ROOF!

592
00:40:50,448 --> 00:40:51,908
I get that you like money,

593
00:40:51,992 --> 00:40:54,411
but how could you do this
without talking to me first?

594
00:40:54,494 --> 00:40:56,413
Come on, bro.

595
00:40:56,496 --> 00:40:59,875
It's not like you two would have to
see each other at work every day.

596
00:40:59,958 --> 00:41:02,502
-Just chill out.
-Chill out?

597
00:41:03,170 --> 00:41:04,004
Chill out?

598
00:41:04,087 --> 00:41:05,380
I want to make money!

599
00:41:09,843 --> 00:41:10,677
I mean,

600
00:41:12,220 --> 00:41:15,891
I don't want to spend my whole life
just looking after you.

601
00:41:17,309 --> 00:41:18,602
We can't let a good opportunity

602
00:41:18,685 --> 00:41:20,729
slip through our fingers
because of how you feel.

603
00:41:22,439 --> 00:41:24,441
Come on, bro.

604
00:41:24,524 --> 00:41:26,902
Gwon Se-na spends
ten months of the entire year abroad.

605
00:41:26,985 --> 00:41:29,237
There's no chance
of running into her at work!

606
00:41:30,280 --> 00:41:31,406
I'm leaving the company.

607
00:41:33,200 --> 00:41:34,075
Bro.

608
00:41:34,701 --> 00:41:35,911
Bro!

609
00:41:41,791 --> 00:41:43,793
EUNSEONG
CHAIRMAN LEE DAE-HO

610
00:41:47,756 --> 00:41:49,174
Why did you meet with Lim Hyeon-jun?

611
00:41:49,257 --> 00:41:51,092
Rumors are flying around the industry.

612
00:41:52,844 --> 00:41:55,430
I can't even get away from you,
and look at the mess I'm in.

613
00:41:55,513 --> 00:41:57,599
What other awful things
are you planning to do?

614
00:41:57,682 --> 00:42:00,477
How long do you plan on using me
before you're satisfied?

615
00:42:10,362 --> 00:42:11,321
How amusing.

616
00:42:43,895 --> 00:42:44,980
HWANG JI-SUN

617
00:42:46,523 --> 00:42:47,399
What?

618
00:42:47,482 --> 00:42:48,400
Hey, bro.

619
00:42:49,317 --> 00:42:50,318
Bro, I…

620
00:42:52,654 --> 00:42:54,030
Just say it.

621
00:42:54,114 --> 00:42:55,740
I'm sorry for
raising my voice at you earlier.

622
00:42:56,283 --> 00:42:58,451
If you're that against it…

623
00:43:00,829 --> 00:43:02,080
I'll call off the merger.

624
00:43:02,163 --> 00:43:04,165
Can you even call it off at this point?

625
00:43:05,166 --> 00:43:07,502
I guess I'll have to
get on my knees and beg.

626
00:43:08,837 --> 00:43:09,713
You're right.

627
00:43:10,338 --> 00:43:12,924
You can't look after me
for the rest of your life.

628
00:43:13,008 --> 00:43:14,009
But don't you dare

629
00:43:14,801 --> 00:43:18,346
get me involved with Gwon Se-na
when it comes to work.

630
00:43:18,430 --> 00:43:20,390
If you do that,
I'll leave for another agency!

631
00:43:21,683 --> 00:43:22,684
Wait, really?

632
00:43:22,767 --> 00:43:24,227
Are you for real?

633
00:43:24,311 --> 00:43:25,186
I'm hanging up!

634
00:43:35,030 --> 00:43:37,866
SPORTS EUNSEONG

635
00:43:39,659 --> 00:43:40,910
Good morning.

636
00:43:40,994 --> 00:43:41,870
Hello.

637
00:44:00,638 --> 00:44:02,640
Isn't Jeong-sin acting strange these days?

638
00:44:03,516 --> 00:44:04,517
Is she?

639
00:44:05,310 --> 00:44:07,437
I have to admit, she's somehow different

640
00:44:07,520 --> 00:44:09,689
from when she first started here.

641
00:44:10,648 --> 00:44:12,567
Look at her. She's grinning.

642
00:44:13,860 --> 00:44:15,195
She's probably seeing someone.

643
00:44:16,321 --> 00:44:17,572
Like, dating.

644
00:44:45,266 --> 00:44:46,768
SOULISHERE (N SEOUL TOWER LOVE LOCKS)
TODAY, 8 P.M.

645
00:45:28,726 --> 00:45:29,561
Hello.

646
00:45:36,609 --> 00:45:37,610
Mr. Lee.

647
00:45:43,992 --> 00:45:46,119
I'm sorry about that night.

648
00:45:50,039 --> 00:45:52,083
Did you really have to
draw the line like that?

649
00:45:52,792 --> 00:45:54,335
I can accept that you didn't show up.

650
00:45:55,044 --> 00:45:56,129
But did you have to…

651
00:45:57,422 --> 00:45:59,841
Did you have to send
someone else in your place?

652
00:45:59,924 --> 00:46:01,968
-Excuse me?
-You got it all wrong.

653
00:46:02,051 --> 00:46:04,637
Chief Yun and I were over a long time ago.

654
00:46:09,809 --> 00:46:11,978
You don't get to decide how I feel.

655
00:47:05,448 --> 00:47:06,407
Hello.

656
00:47:06,491 --> 00:47:07,617
Hello.

657
00:47:07,700 --> 00:47:09,202
Do you believe in the Way?

658
00:47:09,285 --> 00:47:11,496
I see inner turmoil in your face.

659
00:47:11,579 --> 00:47:14,874
Your ancestors are furious right now.

660
00:47:16,251 --> 00:47:17,168
No, no, no!

661
00:47:17,252 --> 00:47:18,711
I'm sure she's not weird like that.

662
00:47:44,988 --> 00:47:47,699
I actually look a lot like Lim Hyeon-jun.

663
00:47:47,782 --> 00:47:49,784
I even sound like him.

664
00:47:49,867 --> 00:47:51,744
"They say you can't fix people."

665
00:47:52,328 --> 00:47:53,746
"But I do."

666
00:47:53,830 --> 00:47:55,498
Wow, how are you so good at impressions?

667
00:47:56,708 --> 00:47:57,792
What am I going to do?

668
00:48:03,756 --> 00:48:07,093
BAK BYEONG-GI

669
00:48:10,597 --> 00:48:12,515
What brings you here all of a sudden?

670
00:48:12,599 --> 00:48:13,600
Oh, I…

671
00:48:13,683 --> 00:48:15,643
The thing is…

672
00:48:16,519 --> 00:48:17,395
Byeong-gi.

673
00:48:18,771 --> 00:48:19,772
I'm here today

674
00:48:20,481 --> 00:48:21,316
because I…

675
00:48:22,150 --> 00:48:24,694
I have a favor to ask you
from one human being to another.

676
00:48:24,777 --> 00:48:26,988
What is it this time?

677
00:48:27,071 --> 00:48:29,115
I took out the romantic lines
with Gwon Se-na

678
00:48:29,198 --> 00:48:31,284
and added a backstory
with your colleague's sister.

679
00:48:31,367 --> 00:48:32,493
What more could you possibly want?

680
00:48:32,577 --> 00:48:33,745
It's not like that.

681
00:48:33,828 --> 00:48:36,164
You don't have to change any of that.

682
00:48:36,247 --> 00:48:38,082
I'll do whatever you write.

683
00:48:38,166 --> 00:48:39,250
What's going on?

684
00:48:39,959 --> 00:48:41,794
I said I had a favor to ask you.

685
00:48:41,878 --> 00:48:45,089
I'll follow the script
if you do me this favor.

686
00:48:48,092 --> 00:48:49,344
Come on, Byeong-gi.

687
00:48:55,558 --> 00:48:56,851
Seriously, your situation

688
00:48:57,810 --> 00:48:59,437
is absolutely wild.

689
00:48:59,520 --> 00:49:00,730
Jeez.

690
00:49:01,898 --> 00:49:04,651
Mr. Lim, can I write a script about this?

691
00:49:04,734 --> 00:49:05,568
Hey!

692
00:49:05,652 --> 00:49:08,946
How can you say that at a time like this?

693
00:49:09,030 --> 00:49:10,448
That's not the point here!

694
00:49:10,531 --> 00:49:12,325
Okay, just calm down.

695
00:49:15,203 --> 00:49:16,079
Seriously…

696
00:49:20,375 --> 00:49:22,210
You're the only one I can ask.

697
00:49:22,293 --> 00:49:24,671
Right, you can't ask Mr. Hwang
because he's married.

698
00:49:24,754 --> 00:49:28,675
I wouldn't ask him for this favor
even if he weren't married.

699
00:49:28,758 --> 00:49:30,259
But won't she be suspicious of me?

700
00:49:30,343 --> 00:49:32,762
You can cover up in clothes,
but not your vibe.

701
00:49:32,845 --> 00:49:35,765
No, it's fine.
We saw each other for less than a minute.

702
00:49:35,848 --> 00:49:38,810
You and I have a similar physique anyway.

703
00:49:39,727 --> 00:49:42,814
-So I just have to say that I'm you?
-Yes.

704
00:49:48,736 --> 00:49:49,737
You'll do it, right?

705
00:49:50,655 --> 00:49:52,532
Come on, Byeong-gi.

706
00:49:53,408 --> 00:49:54,492
You'll do it, right?

707
00:49:54,575 --> 00:49:56,369
Well…

708
00:49:57,662 --> 00:49:58,496
I suppose…

709
00:49:59,080 --> 00:50:00,164
NEW RECORDING 1

710
00:50:00,248 --> 00:50:01,249
…that I could.

711
00:50:04,127 --> 00:50:06,045
Thanks so much, Byeong-gi.

712
00:50:10,633 --> 00:50:12,677
Wait, do you have something on me now?

713
00:50:12,760 --> 00:50:14,971
You already know the answer to that.

714
00:50:17,056 --> 00:50:19,684
Sit back and relax.

715
00:50:21,310 --> 00:50:23,688
After the fifth episode,

716
00:50:23,771 --> 00:50:26,357
there will be a lot of action scenes
that you're not going to like.

717
00:50:28,025 --> 00:50:29,193
How much is a lot?

718
00:50:29,277 --> 00:50:31,028
Nonstop.

719
00:50:35,450 --> 00:50:36,868
I'll do it.

720
00:50:36,951 --> 00:50:39,120
There'll also be a shower scene
that you can't stand.

721
00:50:39,746 --> 00:50:41,122
But my muscles are gone now.

722
00:50:43,791 --> 00:50:44,917
Of course, I'll do it!

723
00:50:45,501 --> 00:50:47,879
I'll do it. No problem.

724
00:50:47,962 --> 00:50:50,214
-And a kissing scene with Ms. Gwon.
-Sure, I'll do it.

725
00:50:51,048 --> 00:50:52,967
Wait, not that!

726
00:50:53,050 --> 00:50:55,595
Some things just can't be done.
I won't do that!

727
00:50:57,096 --> 00:50:59,474
-I guess it can't be helped, then.
-Hold on.

728
00:51:00,266 --> 00:51:01,267
Director Bak.

729
00:51:01,350 --> 00:51:02,643
That's just…

730
00:51:04,520 --> 00:51:05,855
I can't do that.

731
00:51:05,938 --> 00:51:07,857
-Please don't make me.
-Well…

732
00:51:07,940 --> 00:51:11,903
Then why don't you
take your time and think about it?

733
00:51:12,403 --> 00:51:13,446
I'll wait.

734
00:51:15,573 --> 00:51:17,450
It looks like the sun will set soon.

735
00:51:18,951 --> 00:51:20,328
What time do I have to leave by?

736
00:51:21,704 --> 00:51:22,580
What time…

737
00:51:23,414 --> 00:51:24,707
Oh, well.

738
00:51:26,584 --> 00:51:30,379
Why didn't you dress more like a writer?

739
00:51:30,463 --> 00:51:32,548
Writers don't dress any differently.

740
00:51:33,216 --> 00:51:34,801
You know what I mean.

741
00:51:34,884 --> 00:51:37,428
Something formal and refined.

742
00:51:37,512 --> 00:51:40,890
Then why don't you go meet her yourself?

743
00:51:42,767 --> 00:51:46,062
Jeez, I can't stand you.

744
00:51:47,230 --> 00:51:49,816
So how should I act when I get there?

745
00:51:49,899 --> 00:51:51,692
Should I end things today
by acting like a jerk?

746
00:51:51,776 --> 00:51:53,486
Or should I charm her into seeing me?

747
00:51:53,569 --> 00:51:54,695
Charm her?

748
00:51:55,780 --> 00:51:58,449
Is that something you can do
if you set your mind to it?

749
00:51:59,200 --> 00:52:01,035
I'm popular in my own way.

750
00:52:03,079 --> 00:52:04,831
No, don't do stuff like that.

751
00:52:04,914 --> 00:52:06,082
I'm going to end things.

752
00:52:07,667 --> 00:52:09,085
Hand me your phone.

753
00:52:09,168 --> 00:52:10,795
Phone? My phone?

754
00:52:10,878 --> 00:52:14,423
I need to know what you talked about
if I'm going to act like Melomaster.

755
00:52:14,507 --> 00:52:15,424
But…

756
00:52:15,508 --> 00:52:16,926
-Hurry up.
-I get it, but…

757
00:52:17,009 --> 00:52:18,177
Jeez.

758
00:52:39,198 --> 00:52:40,157
Have you got some fun plans?

759
00:52:42,869 --> 00:52:46,122
I'm not sure if it'll be fun
or if I'll end up humiliating myself.

760
00:52:46,205 --> 00:52:48,040
I went to the restaurant that night.

761
00:52:48,541 --> 00:52:50,042
I happened to overhear your conversation.

762
00:52:51,502 --> 00:52:52,420
Why did you do that?

763
00:52:53,462 --> 00:52:54,463
Mr. Lee…

764
00:52:55,131 --> 00:52:57,341
He thinks I sent you there.

765
00:52:57,425 --> 00:53:00,303
We were together
for a long time back in the US.

766
00:53:03,431 --> 00:53:04,473
I know.

767
00:53:05,266 --> 00:53:06,392
How?

768
00:53:06,475 --> 00:53:09,812
The way you act makes it clear
that you still have feelings for him.

769
00:53:11,314 --> 00:53:12,148
Do I?

770
00:53:12,940 --> 00:53:14,525
Going to the restaurant was too much.

771
00:53:14,609 --> 00:53:15,985
You weren't going to show up anyway.

772
00:53:18,821 --> 00:53:21,240
I want to glue our relationship
back together.

773
00:53:23,409 --> 00:53:24,911
I'll wish you good luck instead.

774
00:53:25,411 --> 00:53:28,456
I hope you don't humiliate yourself today,
and something good comes your way.

775
00:53:29,290 --> 00:53:30,291
You've got this.

776
00:53:36,923 --> 00:53:39,175
Why are you reading it so carefully?

777
00:53:39,258 --> 00:53:42,053
There's so much
that I can't even skim through it all.

778
00:53:42,136 --> 00:53:43,179
Then don't look at it.

779
00:53:43,262 --> 00:53:44,680
-Stop reading!
-Wow.

780
00:53:44,764 --> 00:53:47,266
You're basically in a pseudo-relationship.

781
00:53:47,850 --> 00:53:49,060
A pseudo-relationship?

782
00:53:49,143 --> 00:53:52,063
You two have been flirting nonstop,
only you've never actually met.

783
00:53:52,897 --> 00:53:54,690
But why are you trying to end things?

784
00:53:54,774 --> 00:53:57,193
Based on your talks,
she seems totally normal.

785
00:53:58,152 --> 00:53:58,986
Really?

786
00:53:59,070 --> 00:54:02,615
She does seem slightly stiff,

787
00:54:02,698 --> 00:54:04,200
but she's honest and sincere.

788
00:54:04,283 --> 00:54:06,827
She doesn't feel sorry for herself
or get overly emotional.

789
00:54:06,911 --> 00:54:09,830
She's not very good at taking photos,

790
00:54:09,914 --> 00:54:11,916
so she's not addicted to social media.

791
00:54:12,500 --> 00:54:14,210
And her purchases indicate

792
00:54:14,293 --> 00:54:16,003
that her personal life
is perfectly ordinary.

793
00:54:16,087 --> 00:54:17,838
You have a real knack for this, don't you?

794
00:54:18,422 --> 00:54:19,924
-How old is she?
-How should I know?

795
00:54:20,007 --> 00:54:20,967
What's her job?

796
00:54:21,509 --> 00:54:22,635
I don't know.

797
00:54:23,803 --> 00:54:26,180
If she turns out to be great,
why don't you meet her?

798
00:54:29,141 --> 00:54:31,352
If you don't want to go in circles,

799
00:54:31,435 --> 00:54:34,563
maybe it's time to choose a path
and stick with it.

800
00:54:35,523 --> 00:54:37,191
It seems you've
already made up your mind anyway.

801
00:54:38,192 --> 00:54:39,443
No.

802
00:54:39,527 --> 00:54:41,028
I've decided to end things.

803
00:54:41,112 --> 00:54:44,782
So you can't let her know who I really am.

804
00:54:44,865 --> 00:54:49,161
Right, I suppose this situation
can be a bit troublesome for you.

805
00:54:51,580 --> 00:54:52,832
-Gosh.
-Hey!

806
00:54:52,915 --> 00:54:54,792
Quit reading!

807
00:54:55,876 --> 00:54:56,877
Jeez.

808
00:54:56,961 --> 00:54:57,795
Just drive.

809
00:55:14,979 --> 00:55:16,689
I'll be back soon, so stay close by.

810
00:55:17,273 --> 00:55:18,274
Okay.

811
00:55:42,798 --> 00:55:45,176
You didn't have to follow me
all the way here.

812
00:55:45,259 --> 00:55:48,054
You never know.
What if some weirdo shows up?

813
00:55:48,137 --> 00:55:49,346
Seriously.

814
00:55:49,972 --> 00:55:50,890
Onion!

815
00:55:51,515 --> 00:55:52,433
I just arrived.

816
00:55:52,516 --> 00:55:54,435
I'm wearing a pink dress.

817
00:55:55,811 --> 00:55:58,105
-She says she's here.
-Calm down.

818
00:55:58,189 --> 00:55:59,690
I'm the one meeting her.

819
00:55:59,774 --> 00:56:00,900
Right.

820
00:56:01,400 --> 00:56:02,234
You…

821
00:56:03,527 --> 00:56:07,156
You're sure you can pull this off, right?

822
00:56:07,239 --> 00:56:08,616
-Mr. Lim, take a deep breath.
-Yeah?

823
00:56:15,539 --> 00:56:18,375
I'll make it a clean break for you,
so don't worry.

824
00:56:18,459 --> 00:56:19,877
Okay. A clean break.

825
00:56:19,960 --> 00:56:21,754
-A clean break.
-Wait.

826
00:56:23,214 --> 00:56:25,299
Don't hurt her feelings too much.

827
00:56:26,258 --> 00:56:28,094
Right, I'll be back.

828
00:56:28,177 --> 00:56:30,304
-Wait, Byeong-gi!
-What now?

829
00:56:30,387 --> 00:56:32,139
She's wearing a pink dress!

830
00:57:07,800 --> 00:57:08,634
There you are.

831
00:57:34,827 --> 00:57:36,120
Soulishere?

832
00:58:22,583 --> 00:58:24,877
Do you like Lim Hyeon-jun?

833
00:58:25,753 --> 00:58:27,254
It's the first time in my life.

834
00:58:27,838 --> 00:58:30,382
I've never liked someone
so unconditionally.

835
00:59:23,894 --> 00:59:26,105
SPECIAL THANKS TO OH YEON-SEO
FOR HER APPEARANCE

836
00:59:28,607 --> 00:59:30,442
I know that woman is this woman,

837
00:59:30,526 --> 00:59:32,778
but that woman doesn't know
I'm Lim Hyeon-jun.

838
00:59:32,861 --> 00:59:34,822
It's a huge mess.

839
00:59:34,905 --> 00:59:35,906
I just want

840
00:59:36,448 --> 00:59:37,866
to remain friends.

841
00:59:37,950 --> 00:59:40,577
What the hell did you say to her?

842
00:59:40,661 --> 00:59:41,537
What are you talking about?

843
00:59:41,620 --> 00:59:45,791
How could you meet someone on Onion
without even knowing who might show up?

844
00:59:45,874 --> 00:59:48,127
The truth is, there's someone I like.

845
00:59:48,836 --> 00:59:52,089
Isn't it possible she sent someone else,
just like we did?

846
00:59:52,172 --> 00:59:55,509
There's something
I need to check personally.

847
01:00:00,264 --> 01:00:02,266
Subtitle: Jenny Kim

